# .gitignore for TBSS-Signature
#
# Rule of thumb for this repository: source code, source data, the derived
# tables that a README refers to, and every published figure are tracked.
# Downloaded archives, virtual environments, package libraries, and scratch
# files rebuilt by a script are not.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- R
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
.Rproj.user/
Rplots.pdf

# --------------------------------------------------- Editors and OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# ---------------------------------------------------------- Agent tooling
.agents/
.claude/

# ------------------------------------- Stage 6: MIDORI2 sequence archives
# ~700 MB of FASTA archives. Their URLs, sizes, and SHA-256 hashes are in
# 6amino_acid_shift/data/derived_midori/midori_file_manifest.csv; download
# them from reference-midori.info and re-run 6amino_acid_shift/run_analysis.py.
# The derived QC table this stage needs IS tracked, so the notebook runs
# without the archives.
/6amino_acid_shift/data/midori/

# -------------------------- Stage 5 signatures: environments and scratch
# Tracked on purpose: the scripts, reference/triplet_counts_*.json (needed to
# run step 1), results/*.csv, and figures/*. Ignored below: environments and
# files regenerated by 1_run_sigprofiler.py and 2_run_msigact.py.
/5context192/signatures/.venv/
/5context192/signatures/.Rlib/
/5context192/signatures/input/
/5context192/signatures/work/
